{{also|Feminist}}
==English==

===Etymology===
First recorded in English 1852. Ultimately from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|fēminīnus}}, from {{m|la|fēmina||woman}}. See also {{m|en|feminine}}, {{m|en|feminism}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈfɛmənɪst/|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|fem|in|ist|lang=en}}

===Hypernyms===
* {{l|en|egalitarian}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Relating to or in accordance with [[feminism]].
#* {{quote-book
|date=2000-05-01
|author={{w|bell hooks}}
|title={{w|Feminist Theory: From Margin to Center}}
|edition=2nd
|page=xi
|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=uvIQbop4cdsC&pg=PR11
|passage='''Feminist''' struggle takes place anytime anywhere any female or male resists sexism, sexist exploitation, and oppression.
}}

